# `korvyn-agent`

Read [`packages/agent/README.md`](../../packages/agent/README.md) before editing — it is
the full working guide. [`packages/agent/CLAUDE.md`](../../packages/agent/CLAUDE.md) is
the load-bearing summary.

A full agentic layer (not a chatbot) over a compact, deterministic port of the Meridian
fixture (`src/graph.ts`, `src/ledger.ts`), using the Claude API with tool-calling:
streaming, multi-turn, and it **takes action**. It is a separate package specifically so
the LLM dependency and the API key live server-side and neither `apps/` nor
`packages/core/` is touched.

## Must not break

- **It cannot break the ledger.** `post_to_ledger` exists but is **refused by
  construction**: posting needs a `HumanApproval` token whose branding Symbol is
  closure-private, so no agent code path can mint one. The ERP stays the system of record.
  **Do not add a path that mints approval.**
- **The API key never leaves the server.** `.env` is git-ignored; `.env.example` is the
  committed template. Never commit a real key, never surface one to a client.
- AI narrates and acts through tools; it does not compute a figure of its own.

## Check

```bash
cd packages/agent && npm run dryrun   # every tool resolves, no API call
```

Node is not on `PATH` — see the project rule.
